          <i class="fa-solid fa-bullhorn animate-pulse"></i>
          <span>Historic Official Declaration · 18:58 PDT</span>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white leading-relaxed">
          "I now solemnly declare: The San Francisco Chapter of the NACUAA Northern California Chapter is officially founded!"
        </blockquote>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-amber-200/80 leading-relaxed">
          — Proclaimed by Sunny Chen, President of North America Colleges and Universities Alumni Alliance (NACUAA HQ)
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Narrative Content Body -->
      <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800 space-y-3 text-base">
          <p>
            <strong>【North Alpha Post / Silicon Valley】</strong> On the eve of the traditional Chongyang Festival, Saturday evening, October 17, 2026, the international conference hall at California Science and Technology University (CSTU) was brilliantly lit. The long-awaited <strong>NACUAA San Francisco Chapter Founding Ceremony</strong> was grandly held via a hybrid offline-online assembly connecting leaders and alumni from 18 states.
          </p>
          <p>
            The assembly was hosted by <strong>Michael Huo (Mingxu Huo)</strong>, President of the NACUAA Northern California Chapter and Chairman of the AI Entrepreneurship & Public Good Club.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-purple-500 pl-4">
            1. CSTU Welcome Address: Industry-Academia Empowerment
          </h2>
          <p>
            President Qin of California Science and Technology University (CSTU) warmly welcomed attendees and posed a thought-provoking strategic question: <em>"With many alumni associations in North America, what is the unique positioning of NACUAA?"</em>
          </p>
          <p>
            President Qin introduced CSTU's core missions: prioritizing employment, high tech, and student-first education, while offering paid retraining, free youth tech programs, and degrees in AI, robotics, and clean energy.
          </p>
          <p>
            Following the address, <strong>Shi Yi (11)</strong>, CSTU host representative and head of the Silicon Valley Robotics & AI Innovation Center, demonstrated the on-site physical AI robotics laboratory and emphasized CSTU's commitment to supporting alumni ventures.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-4">
            2. President Sunny Chen's Keynote: Regional Governance & Dual-Hub Momentum
          </h2>
          <p>
            NACUAA President <strong>Sunny Chen</strong> delivered the keynote address, congratulating the preparatory team and outlining three core expectations: uniting alumni fellowship, building multidisciplinary platforms, and carrying forward public-benefit service.
          </p>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-blue-950/30 border border-blue-500/30 space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-400 block">★ Authoritative Governance Announcement</span>
            <p class="text-slate-200 italic font-medium">
              "Northern California has a seasoned leadership team. The Silicon Valley Chapter, built under President Qilei Peng, has grown steadily. We now formally unify it under the Northern California regional chapter architecture! Under NorCal, we have the Silicon Valley Chapter, and today we add the vibrant new San Francisco Chapter!"
            </p>
          </div>
          <p>
            This announcement establishes the clear organizational hierarchy: <strong>NorCal Chapter governs regional coordination, with San Francisco Chapter and Silicon Valley Chapter operating as dual growth engines</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Chairman of the Board <strong>Shuhui Peng</strong> also delivered congratulatory remarks, commending Northern California's dynamism in AI Agent applications and pledging full Board support.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-emerald-500 pl-4">
            3. Senior Community Leaders: Elevating the Ambitions of Youth
          </h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/40 border border-slate-800">
              <strong class="text-white">Dr. Quan Li</strong> shared insights on club developments, including AI music video creation and weekly Guandan club sessions bringing alumni together.
            </li>
            <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/40 border border-slate-800">
              <strong class="text-white">Jerry Zhang</strong> (Vice Chairman of the Board) reaffirmed his dedication to providing a solid foundation for young talent.
            </li>
            <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/40 border border-slate-800">
              <strong class="text-white">Qilei Peng</strong> (Founding President of Silicon Valley Chapter):
              <blockquote class="italic text-slate-300 mt-2 pl-3 border-l-2 border-slate-700">
                "San Francisco is the stage for the younger generation. They need not just a social club, but an expansive platform that can truly hold their ambitions. The real value of the SF Chapter is serving as a solid launchpad for their dreams."
              </blockquote>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-pink-500 pl-4">
            4. East-West Coast Alliance: Nationwide Sister Chapters
          </h2>
          <p>
            Editor-in-Chief Mao of the North Carolina Chamber of Commerce highlighted the golden bridge connecting Research Triangle Park with Silicon Valley and San Francisco. NACUAA Deputy Secretary-General HP and representatives from Greater Washington DC, Washington State (Seattle), and Southern California chapters joined online in celebration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-indigo-500 pl-4">
            5. Original AI Music Video Release & President Jane Cheung's Vision
          </h2>
          <p>
            An original celebratory music video written, composed, and synthesized via generative AI by <strong>Michael Huo</strong> was premiered.
          </p>
          <p>
            Subsequently, <strong>Jane Cheung (张建章)</strong>, Inaugural President of the San Francisco Chapter, shared her three core aspirations:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-slate-300 pl-2">
            <li><strong>Connecting Alumni & Rooting in Community</strong>: A warm, authentic intellectual sanctuary;</li>
            <li><strong>Harnessing the Innovation High Ground</strong>: Unlocking SF's edge in AI-native ventures and cross-sector partnerships;</li>
            <li><strong>Open Ecosystem & Mutual Success</strong>: A bridge between nationwide alumni and Silicon Valley tech momentum.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4">
            6. Epilogue: Answering the Strategic Question & 18:58 Proclamation
          </h2>
          <p>
            President Sunny Chen concluded by answering President Qin's opening question on NACUAA's positioning:
          </p>
          <blockquote class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-950/30 border border-amber-500/30 text-amber-100 font-medium italic">
            "What is NACUAA's positioning? We are a nationwide, comprehensive alumni alliance spanning 18 states and two Canadian cities, driven by strategic cross-regional collaboration, mutual empowerment, and deep community integration!"
          </blockquote>
          <p>
            At precisely <strong>18:58 PDT</strong>, President Sunny Chen officially declared the San Francisco Chapter founded, followed by a celebratory virtual group photo with attendees across North America.
          </p>
        </div>

